<?xml version="1.0"?>
<tt xmlns:vt="http://namespace.itunes.apple.com/itt/ttml-extension#vertical" xmlns:ttp="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml#parameter" xmlns:ittp="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml/profile/imsc1#parameter" xmlns:tt_feature="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml/feature/" xmlns:ebutts="urn:ebu:tt:style" xmlns:tts="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml#styling" xmlns:tt_extension="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml/extension/" xmlns:tt_profile="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml/profile/" xmlns:ttm="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml#metadata" xmlns:ry="http://namespace.itunes.apple.com/itt/ttml-extension#ruby" xmlns:itts="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml/profile/imsc1#styling" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml" xml:lang="en-US" ttp:dropMode="nonDrop" ttp:frameRate="60" ttp:frameRateMultiplier="1 1" ttp:timeBase="smpte" xmlns:tt="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <head>
    <styling>
      <style xml:id="normal" tts:color="white" tts:fontFamily="sansSerif" tts:fontSize="100%" tts:fontStyle="normal" tts:fontWeight="normal"/>
    </styling>
    <layout>
      <region xml:id="bottom" tts:displayAlign="after" tts:extent="100% 15%" tts:origin="0% 85%" tts:writingMode="lrtb"/>
    </layout>
  </head>
  <body tts:color="white" region="bottom" style="normal">
    <div>
      <p begin="00:00:00:29" end="00:00:03:25" region="bottom">Hi, my name is Jonathan McMichael.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:03:29" end="00:00:06:15" region="bottom">I am an AS strategist at Arizona State University.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:06:18" end="00:00:08:38" region="bottom">I'm a former librarian, former instructional designer.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:08:42" end="00:00:11:53" region="bottom">Um, I've been working with uh, for the last little bit in</p>
      <p begin="00:00:11:53" end="00:00:12:54" region="bottom"> the AI space.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:12:58" end="00:00:16:16" region="bottom">And recently, a lot of folks have come up to me saying,</p>
      <p begin="00:00:16:16" end="00:00:17:21" region="bottom"> I'm interested in these agents.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:17:24" end="00:00:20:24" region="bottom">I'm seeing Claude Code and Kodex and a lot of news on that.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:20:28" end="00:00:23:28" region="bottom">Can you kind of point me in the direction of some resources</p>
      <p begin="00:00:23:28" end="00:00:25:27" region="bottom"> and tools that help me catch up with what's going on.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:25:30" end="00:00:28:44" region="bottom">One, that's a big daunting test because no one feels like</p>
      <p begin="00:00:28:44" end="00:00:32:09" region="bottom"> everyone feels like they have to catch up and no one feels like they're in a good space.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:32:13" end="00:00:35:20" region="bottom">So, um, but when I went out to Lafond</p>
      <p begin="00:00:35:20" end="00:00:38:27" region="bottom"> some resources, I kind of felt like there were these 2 types of</p>
      <p begin="00:00:38:28" end="00:00:41:28" region="bottom"> patterns and none of them really fit, uh, the types of people that I wanted to</p>
      <p begin="00:00:41:28" end="00:00:43:34" region="bottom"> work with or the types of people who were asking me these questions.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:44:24" end="00:00:47:28" region="bottom">Some of them ended up being very technical because a</p>
      <p begin="00:00:47:28" end="00:00:50:57" region="bottom"> lot of these tools were built around coding and software development.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:51:00" end="00:00:54:00" region="bottom">And some of these tutorials ended up being a</p>
      <p begin="00:00:54:00" end="00:00:56:49" region="bottom"> little bit more like tips and tricks, hacks and stuff like that.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:56:53" end="00:01:00:07" region="bottom">They didn't really get to the big picture of what's going on.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:00:11" end="00:01:03:14" region="bottom">What I was finding is that people were feeling kind of afraid to</p>
      <p begin="00:01:03:14" end="00:01:05:24" region="bottom"> tinker with these tools, were afraid to play with them.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:05:28" end="00:01:08:46" region="bottom">I'm not a coder, so I don't feel like I can use some of these things, or</p>
      <p begin="00:01:08:46" end="00:01:10:30" region="bottom"> I'm really scared about what might happen.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:10:34" end="00:01:13:52" region="bottom">And while you should have some kind of concern around agents</p>
      <p begin="00:01:13:52" end="00:01:16:52" region="bottom"> because they can start taking actions outside of you.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:16:55" end="00:01:19:55" region="bottom">I don't want people to be afraid because long term, that's</p>
      <p begin="00:01:19:55" end="00:01:21:03" region="bottom"> not really where we want to go.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:21:07" end="00:01:24:21" region="bottom">So I'm making a series of tutorials, and this is one of the foundational ones.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:24:25" end="00:01:27:47" region="bottom">to kind of give a sense of what are these agents?</p>
      <p begin="00:01:27:50" end="00:01:28:30" region="bottom">How do they work?</p>
      <p begin="00:01:28:30" end="00:01:30:22" region="bottom">kind of foundationally.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:30:25" end="00:01:32:45" region="bottom">These are design systems, we can understand how they work.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:32:49" end="00:01:35:53" region="bottom">And once we start to have a good kind of mental</p>
      <p begin="00:01:35:53" end="00:01:37:30" region="bottom"> model or schema for how they work.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:37:34" end="00:01:40:48" region="bottom">We'll be able to kind of work with them more confidently,</p>
      <p begin="00:01:40:48" end="00:01:43:52" region="bottom"> troubleshoot when they go in the wrong direction and feel like we're more</p>
      <p begin="00:01:43:52" end="00:01:44:57" region="bottom"> in control of what's going on.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:45:00" end="00:01:46:05" region="bottom">And that's what I want to happen.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:46:12" end="00:01:49:16" region="bottom">I'm trying to distill what my experience has been for the</p>
      <p begin="00:01:49:16" end="00:01:52:27" region="bottom"> last little bit with these agents, especially in the last 6 or 8 months.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:52:30" end="00:01:55:37" region="bottom">And give you kind of a head start to</p>
      <p begin="00:01:55:37" end="00:01:59:17" region="bottom"> kind of make, help you feel a little bit more confident working with them.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:59:20" end="00:02:02:24" region="bottom">So, what I'm working on, what the today's presentation or</p>
      <p begin="00:02:02:24" end="00:02:05:28" region="bottom"> today's tutorial is going to be on the foundations of</p>
      <p begin="00:02:05:28" end="00:02:06:51" region="bottom"> Agent of Carnassus.</p>
      <p begin="00:02:06:54" end="00:02:10:16" region="bottom">We're going to talk how we go from LLMs to chatbots to</p>
      <p begin="00:02:10:16" end="00:02:11:28" region="bottom"> agent harnesses.</p>
      <p begin="00:02:11:31" end="00:02:13:19" region="bottom">And we'll talk about what a harness means.</p>
      <p begin="00:02:13:23" end="00:02:16:23" region="bottom">We might also talk about some other terminology, and I'll try to define myself,</p>
      <p begin="00:02:16:23" end="00:02:17:39" region="bottom"> define what those things mean.</p>
      <p begin="00:02:17:42" end="00:02:20:46" region="bottom">I will also demo how these</p>
      <p begin="00:02:20:46" end="00:02:22:09" region="bottom"> tools kind of work.</p>
      <p begin="00:02:22:12" end="00:02:24:18" region="bottom">So you can kind of get a sense of what they look like in practice as well.</p>
      <p begin="00:02:24:22" end="00:02:27:25" region="bottom">But there's gonna be some pretty complicated pictures on here,</p>
      <p begin="00:02:27:25" end="00:02:28:33" region="bottom"> but I'll try to talk my way through it.</p>
      <p begin="00:02:28:37" end="00:02:30:43" region="bottom">So let's start with first.</p>
      <p begin="00:02:33:47" end="00:02:35:21" region="bottom">The OLM engine.</p>
      <p begin="00:02:35:24" end="00:02:38:38" region="bottom">So I'm going to call this thing an engine, this circular thing right here,</p>
      <p begin="00:02:38:38" end="00:02:39:43" region="bottom"> I'm going to call this an engine.</p>
      <p begin="00:02:39:50" end="00:02:42:54" region="bottom">But what I mean by engine is basically all that</p>
      <p begin="00:02:42:54" end="00:02:45:32" region="bottom"> LLMs do is they take an input or context.</p>
      <p begin="00:02:45:36" end="00:02:47:38" region="bottom">So we can see the sentence here.</p>
      <p begin="00:02:47:42" end="00:02:50:24" region="bottom">Trisha spilled our coffee, Dan dot dot dot.</p>
      <p begin="00:02:50:28" end="00:02:53:28" region="bottom">And they do a bunch of</p>
      <p begin="00:02:53:28" end="00:02:56:28" region="bottom"> complicated math, multiplying a bunch of numbers</p>
      <p begin="00:02:56:28" end="00:02:59:42" region="bottom"> by each other, and they come up with what they think, the</p>
      <p begin="00:02:59:42" end="00:03:03:04" region="bottom"> next predicted outcome would be, the Y output,</p>
      <p begin="00:03:03:04" end="00:03:04:34" region="bottom"> the completion or the response.</p>
      <p begin="00:03:04:37" end="00:03:07:55" region="bottom">So we might have at the end of this sentence, jumped up to get a rag.</p>
      <p begin="00:03:07:59" end="00:03:11:24" region="bottom">And so, these are</p>
      <p begin="00:03:11:24" end="00:03:14:28" region="bottom"> really powerful tools, but it doesn't seem that exciting when</p>
      <p begin="00:03:14:28" end="00:03:16:30" region="bottom"> you say, well, it just completes a sentence for us.</p>
      <p begin="00:03:16:34" end="00:03:17:32" region="bottom">How could that be that useful?</p>
      <p begin="00:03:17:35" end="00:03:18:47" region="bottom">Turns out they're really useful.</p>
      <p begin="00:03:18:50" end="00:03:22:08" region="bottom">But for them to be useful, we have to put them inside of</p>
      <p begin="00:03:22:08" end="00:03:25:22" region="bottom"> pieces of software or build things around them so</p>
      <p begin="00:03:25:23" end="00:03:28:44" region="bottom"> that we can take advantage of the really great utility</p>
      <p begin="00:03:28:44" end="00:03:31:55" region="bottom"> of being able to generate language in an effective way.</p>
      <p begin="00:03:31:59" end="00:03:34:59" region="bottom">And so what we call the things we build around them or what we're</p>
      <p begin="00:03:34:59" end="00:03:37:59" region="bottom"> going to call certainly going to call them in this video, um, is</p>
      <p begin="00:03:37:59" end="00:03:39:07" region="bottom"> harnesses.</p>
      <p begin="00:03:39:11" end="00:03:41:17" region="bottom">So this is a harness that we build around that.</p>
      <p begin="00:03:41:20" end="00:03:45:03" region="bottom">So you're going to see this LLM engine powers everything.</p>
      <p begin="00:03:45:07" end="00:03:47:24" region="bottom">These are things like GPT 5.5.</p>
      <p begin="00:03:47:35" end="00:03:49:37" region="bottom">Claude 4.8.</p>
      <p begin="00:03:49:48" end="00:03:52:05" region="bottom">Uh, Gemini 3.5.</p>
      <p begin="00:03:52:19" end="00:03:53:31" region="bottom">These numbered things.</p>
      <p begin="00:03:53:35" end="00:03:57:00" region="bottom">These are the models that we're going to kind of call LLM</p>
      <p begin="00:03:57:00" end="00:03:58:44" region="bottom"> engines that power our harnesses.</p>
      <p begin="00:03:58:48" end="00:04:02:53" region="bottom">And I'm going to talk today a little bit about what these harnesses are.</p>
      <p begin="00:04:02:56" end="00:04:05:27" region="bottom">So I'm going to make the argument that the 1st harness that we had.</p>
      <p begin="00:04:05:35" end="00:04:07:41" region="bottom">was the OG chat harness.</p>
      <p begin="00:04:07:44" end="00:04:10:48" region="bottom">So when chat GPT comes out, this is the 1st</p>
      <p begin="00:04:10:48" end="00:04:14:49" region="bottom"> time LLM engines, these LLM models had existed before.</p>
      <p begin="00:04:14:53" end="00:04:18:07" region="bottom">There had been plenty of LLM models before, GPT</p>
      <p begin="00:04:18:07" end="00:04:21:21" region="bottom"> one, two, when ChatGPT came out, they were running GPT3.</p>
      <p begin="00:04:21:32" end="00:04:24:50" region="bottom">Um, and really what the big innovation</p>
      <p begin="00:04:24:50" end="00:04:27:57" region="bottom"> was was they put a few elements around</p>
      <p begin="00:04:27:58" end="00:04:31:05" region="bottom"> the LM engine and made it function like a chatbot.</p>
      <p begin="00:04:31:08" end="00:04:34:08" region="bottom">The elements they put around it are one, a system prompt.</p>
      <p begin="00:04:34:12" end="00:04:37:44" region="bottom">They kind of stuck a thing on the front end of every interaction</p>
      <p begin="00:04:37:44" end="00:04:40:22" region="bottom"> that told the model.</p>
      <p begin="00:04:40:26" end="00:04:42:10" region="bottom">Hey, you're about to engage with a chat.</p>
      <p begin="00:04:42:14" end="00:04:44:20" region="bottom">You're going to be a helpful assistant.</p>
      <p begin="00:04:44:24" end="00:04:47:31" region="bottom">You're going to respond to the chat as though</p>
      <p begin="00:04:47:31" end="00:04:50:31" region="bottom"> you, as though to be</p>
      <p begin="00:04:50:31" end="00:04:53:27" region="bottom"> helpful to the users in whatever way you see fit.</p>
      <p begin="00:04:53:35" end="00:04:57:00" region="bottom">And the next message you're going to get is going to be that user message.</p>
      <p begin="00:04:57:04" end="00:05:00:11" region="bottom">So when you 1st started a chat, that wasn't the 1st</p>
      <p begin="00:05:00:11" end="00:05:02:35" region="bottom"> thing the LLM engine read, it was the system prompt.</p>
      <p begin="00:05:03:25" end="00:05:06:29" region="bottom">After that, you would</p>
      <p begin="00:05:06:29" end="00:05:09:29" region="bottom"> get the user message, and they would take all of that stuff, and</p>
      <p begin="00:05:09:29" end="00:05:12:58" region="bottom"> if we go back to our model, the X here, all of that was X.</p>
      <p begin="00:05:13:37" end="00:05:17:09" region="bottom">Put that into the LLM engine and then you'd get a response.</p>
      <p begin="00:05:17:13" end="00:05:20:13" region="bottom">It would respond in a pattern of being a chatbot</p>
      <p begin="00:05:20:13" end="00:05:22:37" region="bottom"> and say, hey, here's my response to that thing.</p>
      <p begin="00:05:22:41" end="00:05:25:48" region="bottom">So if you were to have multiple turns to say,</p>
      <p begin="00:05:25:48" end="00:05:27:40" region="bottom"> okay, I want to respond to what they just told me.</p>
      <p begin="00:05:28:01" end="00:05:31:01" region="bottom">The way they kind of, the other thing they</p>
      <p begin="00:05:31:01" end="00:05:34:08" region="bottom"> had to build around that was a way to take that response, take</p>
      <p begin="00:05:34:08" end="00:05:37:15" region="bottom"> it and put it onto the end of the conversation</p>
      <p begin="00:05:37:16" end="00:05:40:34" region="bottom"> history, and then take that whole conversation history, including</p>
      <p begin="00:05:40:34" end="00:05:43:23" region="bottom"> the new messages, and put them back through the LLM.</p>
      <p begin="00:05:43:26" end="00:05:46:33" region="bottom">If you look at our example here, you'll have the system prompt up top, then</p>
      <p begin="00:05:46:34" end="00:05:49:38" region="bottom"> you'll have the user message, and then everything here is that X</p>
      <p begin="00:05:49:38" end="00:05:52:41" region="bottom"> input, and then we get the response Y down here.</p>
      <p begin="00:05:52:44" end="00:05:55:04" region="bottom">So can you summarize this webpage?</p>
      <p begin="00:05:55:08" end="00:05:58:12" region="bottom">To be helpful, I need to see the content of the webpage.</p>
      <p begin="00:05:58:16" end="00:06:02:32" region="bottom">I don't have any tool, like the LLM could say, I don't have any tools to use that web page.</p>
      <p begin="00:06:02:35" end="00:06:05:53" region="bottom">And it would paste that it would say you</p>
      <p begin="00:06:05:53" end="00:06:08:56" region="bottom"> have to paste that content in, so you would paste that content in, and</p>
      <p begin="00:06:08:56" end="00:06:11:38" region="bottom"> then to say, great, here's a summary, and that would be the last response.</p>
      <p begin="00:06:11:42" end="00:06:14:42" region="bottom">But each one of these things gets fed all the way back in.</p>
      <p begin="00:06:14:46" end="00:06:18:08" region="bottom">So the response from the 1st turn, goes</p>
      <p begin="00:06:18:08" end="00:06:21:39" region="bottom"> into the transcript history, and we feed the whole thing back into the LLM engine.</p>
      <p begin="00:06:21:43" end="00:06:24:54" region="bottom">That was the 1st way in which we harnessed LLM,</p>
      <p begin="00:06:24:54" end="00:06:27:54" region="bottom"> uh, engines, that the completion was for an</p>
      <p begin="00:06:27:54" end="00:06:30:18" region="bottom"> entire transcript of a conversation.</p>
      <p begin="00:06:30:22" end="00:06:32:28" region="bottom">So it was role-playing the conversation with you.</p>
      <p begin="00:06:32:31" end="00:06:35:06" region="bottom">And that's the 1st time we harnessed a chat bot.</p>
      <p begin="00:06:35:10" end="00:06:36:22" region="bottom">Okay?</p>
      <p begin="00:06:36:29" end="00:06:39:47" region="bottom">So, things started to evolve,</p>
      <p begin="00:06:39:47" end="00:06:43:19" region="bottom"> and a couple things started to happen, and</p>
      <p begin="00:06:43:19" end="00:06:47:06" region="bottom"> we had the reasoning chatbot harnessed was the next kind of evolution.</p>
      <p begin="00:06:47:10" end="00:06:51:15" region="bottom">We still had chatbots, we still see here that we've got the system prompt.</p>
      <p begin="00:06:52:16" end="00:06:53:53" region="bottom">Uh here.</p>
      <p begin="00:06:53:53" end="00:06:57:00" region="bottom">We have the system prompt here.</p>
      <p begin="00:06:57:04" end="00:07:00:18" region="bottom">We've got our responses, we've</p>
      <p begin="00:07:00:18" end="00:07:02:31" region="bottom"> got our conversation, and we've got our LLM engine.</p>
      <p begin="00:07:02:35" end="00:07:03:15" region="bottom">All of those are the same.</p>
      <p begin="00:07:03:18" end="00:07:04:59" region="bottom">Same pattern of appending to the history.</p>
      <p begin="00:07:05:02" end="00:07:09:07" region="bottom">We've added 2 green elements, tools and descriptions, and reasoning.</p>
      <p begin="00:07:09:11" end="00:07:12:51" region="bottom">So I've combined 2 things that kind of happened in</p>
      <p begin="00:07:12:51" end="00:07:16:30" region="bottom"> close successions to each other, but they were 2 different innovations.</p>
      <p begin="00:07:16:34" end="00:07:19:16" region="bottom">One innovation is the reasoning component.</p>
      <p begin="00:07:19:23" end="00:07:22:55" region="bottom">So reasoning, uh,</p>
      <p begin="00:07:22:55" end="00:07:26:09" region="bottom"> was the ability for the LLM to</p>
      <p begin="00:07:26:10" end="00:07:29:28" region="bottom"> pause, talk to itself 1st and</p>
      <p begin="00:07:29:28" end="00:07:30:51" region="bottom"> then respond back to the user.</p>
      <p begin="00:07:30:58" end="00:07:33:18" region="bottom">That turned out to be really, really effective.</p>
      <p begin="00:07:33:22" end="00:07:37:52" region="bottom">These are things called reasoning traces, that it was able to respond back to the user with.</p>
      <p begin="00:07:37:55" end="00:07:40:55" region="bottom">And that become a way in which it would</p>
      <p begin="00:07:40:55" end="00:07:42:50" region="bottom"> say, oh, the user is asking me to do this.</p>
      <p begin="00:07:43:01" end="00:07:45:29" region="bottom">They want to summary this webpage.</p>
      <p begin="00:07:45:32" end="00:07:47:49" region="bottom">I should use some of the tools that I have to be able to do that.</p>
      <p begin="00:07:47:53" end="00:07:50:56" region="bottom">So that ended up being a new</p>
      <p begin="00:07:50:56" end="00:07:53:56" region="bottom"> way the LM could generate text, but that text didn't go to the</p>
      <p begin="00:07:53:56" end="00:07:55:40" region="bottom"> user into the transcript here.</p>
      <p begin="00:07:55:44" end="00:07:58:58" region="bottom">It went to itself, and it made it a little bit better responding</p>
      <p begin="00:07:58:59" end="00:08:00:07" region="bottom"> at certain types of questions.</p>
      <p begin="00:08:00:11" end="00:08:03:22" region="bottom">The 2nd thing soon after we had reasoning,</p>
      <p begin="00:08:03:22" end="00:08:05:21" region="bottom"> started the ability for it to use tools.</p>
      <p begin="00:08:05:24" end="00:08:08:24" region="bottom">These were a thing called so there's</p>
      <p begin="00:08:08:24" end="00:08:09:40" region="bottom"> this term called runtime.</p>
      <p begin="00:08:09:43" end="00:08:12:43" region="bottom">Basically a runtime, is the ability for a</p>
      <p begin="00:08:12:43" end="00:08:15:25" region="bottom"> set of commands to do a thing on your computer.</p>
      <p begin="00:08:15:29" end="00:08:18:47" region="bottom">It has the ability to run a process and make a thing happen.</p>
